      "writtenOn": "2023-04-17T22:20:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This looks good to me, as is. I had no idea about the `dump` and `cmd` plumbing. This is nice.\n\nI also don\u0027t see much value in moving the code into rkpd. As you point out, that adds more API stability burden.\n\nThe only benefit of moving the impl into rkpd that I can see is that we could more easily extend the commands via mainline update. However, since this is primarily intended for use in the factory, it\u0027s stuck with whatever commands are available in the factory image anyway.\n\nIf we decide to go this route, I assume you\u0027ll be adding some tests.",
      "parentUuid": "403018e5_db11b114",
      "revId": "fc84791e8fc44a38fda804fe4577eec6dd9910e5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
